{{!-- Character, order and apostate secrets. They are standing permissions
      rather than things you cast — "ways to do things you shouldn't be able to
      do normally" — but they are consulted mid-cast, so they sit with the
      practices they modify. House secrets are augments and live with the
      House. --}}
<div class="isun-panel secrets-strip mt-4">
  {{!-- No add button. A secret is taught, researched or stumbled upon — never
        browsed for — so a player has no occasion to reach for one, and the GM
        granting it can hand over the item itself. Dropping a Secret on the
        sheet still works, which is the route that matches how they are
        actually acquired. --}}
  <div class="entry-list-header">
    <h3>{{localize "ISUN.Secrets"}}</h3>
  </div>
  <div class="secret-chips">
    {{#each characterSecrets as |s|}}
      {{!-- Removing a secret is the GM's to do. A secret is bought with Acumen
            and cannot be un-bought, so a one-click delete beside the name is a
            mistake waiting to happen for the player who owns it. --}}
      <span class="secret-chip {{s.system.secretType}}" data-item-id="{{s.id}}">
        <a data-action="open-item" data-item-id="{{s.id}}">{{s.name}}</a>
        {{#if @root.isGM}}
          <a class="item-delete" title="{{localize 'ISUN.Remove'}}" data-action="item-delete"><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i></a>
        {{/if}}
      </span>
    {{else}}
      <span class="empty-state">{{localize "ISUN.NoSecrets"}}</span>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
</div>
